WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.437
The federal requirement.

2
00:00:01.437 --> 00:00:05.774
In NIST special publication
eight hundred fifty-three terms,

3
00:00:05.774 --> 00:00:11.556
this gate supports C A seven, continuous
monitoring with system-level metrics, and

4
00:00:11.556 --> 00:00:16.913
A U six and A U eleven with S I twelve:
the review and retention of audit records.

5
00:00:16.913 --> 00:00:21.525
It also supports BOD 25-01's
continuous reporting.

6
00:00:21.525 --> 00:00:25.700
Your organization still sets the
organization-defined parameters,

7
00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:28.850
and the assessor decides
whether each is satisfied.

8
00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:33.579
The evidence an ISSO keeps for
Gate 7: every period's manifest,

9
00:00:33.579 --> 00:00:38.025
summary and checksum file,
with the approved thresholds.

10
00:00:38.025 --> 00:00:42.800
The packages, with each unauthorized-write
finding's closure at the source.

11
00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:46.527
The storage container's retention
and immutability settings,

12
00:00:46.527 --> 00:00:48.175
set to the records schedule.

13
00:00:48.175 --> 00:00:50.800
And the ScubaGear results
beside the period.

14
00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:56.280
The guide's Evidence section gathers all
seven gates into one file per population.
